From ac9411b42f318f1067eafcd72a1c7a77a6e3c0c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:56:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] llama, server : capture context checkpoints inside a batch

llama-server ends the prompt batch at every context checkpoint (4 and
4+n_ubatch tokens before the end, user message starts) and reads the
state between llama_decode() calls. On a multi-device split each break
drains the pipeline, and the n_ubatch-token call in between runs one
device at a time: on gabesrv10+gabesrv06 (RPC) a 1.9K-token prompt took
9.3 s where llama-bench needs ~6.6 s.

New (experimental) API: llama_state_seq_capture_add(ctx, seq, pos,
flags) asks the next llama_decode() calls to capture the state of seq
right after the token at pos. The batch allocator ends the ubatch there
(an explicit cut also satisfies the recurrent rollback tail, since
prompt tokens are never rolled back into), and the state's tensor
ranges are copied into device buffers with ggml_backend_tensor_copy_async
on the owning backend, ordered between that ubatch and the next.
llama_state_seq_capture_get() reads them back in the
llama_state_seq_get_data_ext() format. Layouts that can't be copied
this way (partial quant blocks, transposed-V row explosion) are refused
by capture_add, so callers can fall back.

The server registers captures instead of breaking the batch and turns
them into checkpoints after the decode, with the same checks a batch
start gets. The draft context is captured too unless it can be trimmed
back (partial seq_rm), in which case it is read after the batch and
trimmed on restore as before. eagle3 keeps splitting (its boundary
state is per batch). LLAMA_SERVER_CKPT_CAPTURE=0 restores the old
behavior.

Results (Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_XL):
- slot saves (KV, recurrent state, checkpoint appendix) byte-identical
  to the split behavior when the ubatch boundaries match, on one GPU and
  over RPC, including a restore from a captured checkpoint
- 20/80 RPC split, 1.9K prompt: 206 -> 262 t/s (llama-bench: ~287)
- single 8060S: +20-40% on 0.2-3.6K prompts

tests: test-state-capture compares captures in one decode against
states read between decodes ending at the same positions (single seq,
two seqs, q8_0 KV full state, retake after re-decode), for qwen35 and
nemotron_h.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
